      "statement": "The MCP server writes a line to a notices file for each refusal it returns, handing the line to one background thread so that the caller returns at once, but neither way out of the serve loop (the normal end and the client hanging up) waits for that thread, so a refusal answered just as the client disconnects can be lost before the panel ever shows it. How is that background notice queue built, how does the server\u0027s serve path end today, and what do the server\u0027s documentation and its open plan currently promise about every refusal leaving a line?",
